# IRIS IRC Protocol License 1.0

**Copyright © 2026 IRIS IRC Project**

## 1. Permission

Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person or organization
to implement, use, reproduce, document, test, extend, and distribute
implementations of the **IRIS IRC Protocol**, subject to the terms of this
license.

This permission includes both non-commercial and commercial use.

## 2. Independent Implementations

Anyone may create an independent implementation of the IRIS IRC Protocol.

An implementation:

* may be open source or proprietary;
* may be commercial or non-commercial;
* may be modified or extended;
* may be implemented in any programming language;
* may run independently of the official IRIS IRC software.

Use of the protocol does not require the implementation to use the IRIS IRC
source code.

## 3. Protocol Extensions

Implementations may extend the IRIS IRC Protocol with additional commands,
messages, capabilities, authentication mechanisms, services, or other
functionality.

Extensions should not be presented as part of the official IRIS IRC
Protocol unless they have been accepted by the IRIS IRC Project.

Implementations should clearly document protocol extensions that are not part
of the official specification.

## 4. Compatibility

An implementation may claim compatibility with the IRIS IRC Protocol only
to the extent that it actually implements the relevant parts of the
specification.

The IRIS IRC Project does not guarantee compatibility between independently
developed implementations.

## 5. Name and Branding

The names:

**IRIS IRC**

and

**IRIS IRC Protocol**

refer to the original project and protocol specification.

Use of these names must not falsely imply that an independent implementation
is developed, maintained, certified, or endorsed by the IRIS IRC Project.

Independent implementations may state, for example:

> "Implements the IRIS IRC Protocol."

but must not imply:

> "Official IRIS IRC Server"

without permission from the IRIS IRC Project.

## 6. No Restriction on Implementation

This license does not require an implementation to publish its source code.

A proprietary or closed-source implementation of the IRIS IRC Protocol is
permitted.

## 7. No Warranty

THE IRIS IRC PROTOCOL SPECIFICATION IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF
ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED.

THE IRIS IRC PROJECT AND ITS AUTHORS SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY DAMAGES,
LOSSES, SECURITY ISSUES, SERVICE INTERRUPTIONS, OR OTHER LIABILITY ARISING
FROM THE USE OR IMPLEMENTATION OF THE PROTOCOL.

## 8. Specification Changes

The IRIS IRC Project may publish new versions of the IRIS IRC Protocol
specification.

Existing implementations are not required to adopt a newer specification
unless they choose to do so.

Protocol versions should be explicitly identified where compatibility may
differ.

## 9. License Notice

A copy of this license should accompany substantial redistributions of the
IRIS IRC Protocol specification.

Implementations are not required to include this license in their source
code merely because they implement the protocol.

